I grew up in a suburb of Detroit  Farmington Hills Michigan I am the  youngest of three and the daughter of a  Lithuanian father and a German mother I  was a big geek  I loved my classes I loved studying I  loved learning and also understand being  the daughter of an immigrant that work  ethic is something that was instilled in  me when I was finishing up at Hillsdale  I knew that I wanted to work in the  music industry so my choices at that  time were either New York or LA and I  moved to Los Angeles with sixty three  dollars and a smith-corona typewriter  and I am not joking I was offered an  internship with a legendary songwriter  Desmond child Desmond was the mastermind  behind the songs for Bon Jovi and  Aerosmith and Cher and Michael Bolton  this was this time period he is one of  my greatest mentors he sold over 300  million albums when he was moving his  operation to Miami I wanted to stay in  LA  and he said you're gonna start your own  company and I had nothing mind you but  what I did have was some knowledge from  Hillsdale where they had discussed being  an owner versus being an employee and  not only in a business sense but being  an owner of your own destiny I was  always asking my clients okay tell me  what's the story before we would go into  an interview before they would write a  song I would say okay tell me what's the  story let's really distill this down and  then one day one of my music clients  turned to me  okay so Petty's what's your story and  the truth was I knew part of my story I  knew that my father was born in  Lithuania and that in 1940 the Soviets  occupied the country I did not know that  it was estimated you know that over 14  million people lost their lives in  Siberia so I decided that I wanted to  tell that story and the idea came pretty  quickly one girl her dream of freedom  and a voice to speak for these millions  of people who never had a chance to  share their story and that became my  first novel my first novel had a lot of  interest to be adapted into a film so we  shot the film in Lithuania imagine the  thrill of seeing a story that you wrote  come to life in the most beautiful way  the film is full of hope and hardship  and strength and struggle and now we're  meeting with distributors and and  submitting to film festivals and so I'm  really excited being honored in this way  by Hillsdale College is indescribable so  much of who I am and what I put into my  work comes from things that I learned  when I was at the school and comes from  people who I admire so deeply it's an  incredibly humbling experience  and I hope I can continue to learn and  grow and create work that moves people  and that people feel is meaningful
 

